# Ship every change

Every change in this repo goes live unless the user explicitly says not to publish (e.g. "don't deploy", "keep it local", "just a branch").

When you finish a change:

1. Verify it: `npm run build` must succeed, and for game changes load the game (`npx vite` in the game folder) and check it renders.
2. Commit to `main` with a clear message.
3. `git push origin main`. The `Deploy to keikigames.com` GitHub Action builds the site and deploys it to the Cloudflare Pages project `keikigames` (https://keikigames.com).
4. Confirm the deploy: `gh run watch $(gh run list -L 1 --json databaseId -q '.[0].databaseId') --exit-status`, then check the changed page on https://keikigames.com.

If the Action is failing or unavailable, deploy manually from the repo root with `set -a && source .env && set +a && npm run deploy`.

If the user says not to publish, commit on a separate branch (or leave uncommitted if asked) and do not push to `main`.
